data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":96,"item_id":"rs_00bae09ac6674cce016ac9f7b806448196bf0231de5cbbb219","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Exploring test setup options**\n\nI need to run some tests, but without a browser available. I guess I could explore using Node with a spawned port set to 0. Maybe I should create a server that allocates a port via the net library and release it afterward, or I could go with a child server that also uses port 0. I think adding a log for useful port dynamics during the test would help parse stdout. It seems easier to allocate a net port and spawn like this."}

